  "definition_equivalence_reviewed": true,
  "review_flags_scope": "The five cyclic relabelling and unordered-support modules, with inspected inherited definitions and proofs. No complete def:walls acceptance.",
  "reason": "I read all five new modules and their theorem types and proof bodies against the full named-wall definition and the explicit labelled/equivariant formalization convention. The implemented branch is faithful: relabelling preserves the actual germs, geometric supports, temporal sign changes and named side conventions; K emptiness uses the actual cyclic visit successor; T/C definitions are independent of any ordered presentation of their actual unordered support. No extra central genericity, differentiability, arbitrary adjacency relation, or assumed support cardinality is introduced into a source-facing theorem.",
  "findings": [
    "The index action is consistently old i to new i−r for shift r P(i)=P(i+r). Support translation is proved injective using its explicit inverse, so singleton and empty zero/concurrence equations are equivalent, not merely transported in one direction. Turn, contact and arbitrary three-label supports, ContactSeparated and NoConsecutive retain their exact modular meanings. The edgeParameter formula is the actual Cramer formula with shifted tuple and shifted ordered edge labels. It is not an abstract parameter supplied to the theorem.",
    "NamedWallRelabel proves iff statements for all six actual source predicates. F/K keep their n≥4 condition, singleton point-zero support, empty concurrence, interior/exterior central geometry and actual turn SignChanges. V/E keep the four excluded contact labels, actual interior or supporting-line/outside-closed-segment condition, and ordered contact chi SignChanges. T retains all three actual ordered parameter-difference SignChanges. C retains its unordered NoConsecutive condition and actual chi SignChanges. The inherited germ relabel leaves the time interval and positive/negative sides unchanged and simply shifts the actual continuous curve. Thus these iff results do not reverse parameter time or orientation.",
    "F right/left conventions are preserved for the same side Bool by the actual shifted turn identity, including their universal quantification over side parameters. V BigonAt and SlidingAt preserve the central neighbour-sign equality/inequality with both neighbour labels shifted correctly. contactSign_relabel preserves the actual negative-side contact sign. This does not assert that an oriented contact sign is determined solely by the centre or identify the F right side with negative time.",
    "CuspRelabel transports the genuine two mutually exclusive central strict-betweenness cases with the same Bool. The first, last and corner labels all translate by −r; in particular the newborn unordered edge pair is the same geometric pair in the shifted representative. The arbitrary-tuple IsCrossing support iff is obtained from the actual crossingShift/crossingUnshift constructions, so it also handles closed-segment contact meanings without an unwarranted central Generic premise. cuspLoopSide_relabel preserves the choice defined by actual newborn crossing membership on the positive side at sideBase. The complementary no-loop side consequently remains the same opposite parameter side.",
    "visitShift_twoStepFirst and visitShift_twoStepLast prove equality of actual sigma visits by their crossing supports and edge labels, including modular wraparound. twoStep_adjacent_shift instantiates the already inspected full Gauss cycle shift theorem and actual successor transport with those endpoint identities. TwoStepAdjacent is a transparent abbreviation exposing the same GenericTuple and edge index; it neither supplies an adjacency hypothesis nor replaces the actual Gauss cycle. cuspEmptyAt_relabel_of_cusp uses the proved central case and loop-side compatibility, then the actual visit-adjacency iff. The unrestricted cuspEmptyAt_relabel also handles non-cusps: CuspEmptyAt contains a cusp witness, and the already proved cusp predicate iff excludes such a witness on either representative. No hidden cusp hypothesis is needed for the final iff.",
    "UnorderedWallTriples first proves sign-change invariance under negation by the exact product identity and under swapping a real difference by pointwise negation. Hence the T parameter-difference conditions survive both a cyclic permutation and the last-label transposition, including the reversed difference on the appropriate edge. The C chi conditions use the actual chirotope cyclic and alternating identities with the correct real coercion. All geometric support conditions are equalities of actual Finsets.",
    "The source-facing tripleAt_support_iff and pureCutAt_support_iff apply to ANY equality of unordered supports. The helper three_support_predicate enumerates the six distinct presentations after deriving each new label belongs to the old support and ruling out repetitions by card=3. Crucially card=3 is not an extra source premise: T derives it from membership in the actual concurrence set forced by its singleton equation; C derives it from the actual singleton point-zero data. Duplicate-label presentations cannot silently satisfy a source wall predicate. Thus the final statements are stronger interfaces than generator-only permutation lemmas, without strengthening the source domain."
  ],
  "not_certified": [
    "The original def:walls row remains pending and receives no original proof or checklist increment from this partial report.",
    "The final aggregate binding every definition, six-way exclusivity, centre determination, all conventions, silent naming and existential kind/simple transport still needs its own complete-source review and current semantic/type/axiom receipt. Any newly assembled WallKindRelabel or aggregate module is outside this five-module partial review.",
    "No classification of arbitrary singular centres as simple, no converse from central conditions to SignChanges, and no main corner state-sum wall law or soft theorem is certified."
  ],
